{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "scripts/backtest_orb.py imports execution_costs and applies a slippage term (in points, unit-reconciled) in addition to FEE_POINTS_ROUNDTRIP.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-E3-ORB-NO-SLIPPAGE", "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "checklist E3 build lane, session_01HmQgaLfZv9rv7uuWfgA321", "rerun": "grep -n \"FEE_POINTS_ROUNDTRIP\\|slippage\\|execution_costs\" scripts/backtest_orb.py"}, "routed_to": null, "state": "queued", "terminal_reason": null, "what": "checklist E3 (cost model reaching every harness): scripts/backtest_orb.py has NO slippage model and was never wired to execution_costs.py. Its fee is modelled in POINTS round-trip (FEE_POINTS_ROUNDTRIP=0.5), not bps -- a deliberate, venue-correct choice for index futures -- but that means execution_costs.roundtrip_cost_r cannot be reused as-is (it assumes a bps-of-notional fee/slippage term). E3 wired the 6 harnesses that had literally zero cost terms (chop_scalp, funding_carry, fvg_range, pairs, xsec_momentum, vwap) plus confirmed the 6 harnesses already wired to execution_costs (fade, ict_scalp, pullback, squeeze, system, trend) resolve slippage/funding via the venue-aware CLI default already. orb.py was NOT wired: it needs a points-vs-bps unit reconciliation (execution_costs.slippage_bps_roundtrip_for(symbol) converted to points via the traded contract's tick/point value) before a slippage term can be added without fabricating a wrong-unit cost."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "src/backtest/backtester.py imports execution_costs and its fee/slippage/funding computation is derived from it (fee_bps_roundtrip / slippage_bps_roundtrip / funding_bps_per_window), not a separate pct-based literal set.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-E3-BACKTESTER-DUAL-COST-MODEL", "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "checklist E3 build lane, session_01HmQgaLfZv9rv7uuWfgA321", "rerun": "grep -n \"taker_fee_pct\\|maker_fee_pct\\|slippage_pct\\|execution_costs\" src/backtest/backtester.py"}, "routed_to": null, "state": "queued", "terminal_reason": null, "what": "checklist E3: src/backtest/backtester.py::ICTBacktester (used by bin/backtest_ict.py, and load_data()/summarize() from it are imported by src/backtest/run_backtest_vwap.py) hardcodes its OWN independent cost model (taker_fee_pct=0.055, maker_fee_pct=0.02, slippage_pct=0.02 at the top of the file) and never imports or consults src/runtime/execution_costs.py -- the exact \"a second cost model is how the two drift\" failure execution_costs.py's own module docstring warns about (P1 section 3.B, the cost-model-single-owner guard family). bin/backtest_ict.py is declared scaffolding-only in its own docstring and has no funding term at all (crypto perp funding never modelled). Not fixed in E3 because changing backtester.py's cost math is a bigger consolidation (rebasing it onto execution_costs.roundtrip_cost_usd) that deserves its own review of whether existing backtester.py consumers depend on the current pct-based numbers."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "scripts/backtest_xsec_momentum.py charges a funding cost per rebalance period (or a dated decision doc explicitly excludes it with a stated reason).", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-E3-XSEC-MOMENTUM-FUNDING-GAP", "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "checklist E3 build lane, session_01HmQgaLfZv9rv7uuWfgA321", "rerun": "grep -n \"FUNDING_BPS_PER_WINDOW\\|funding_bps_per_window\\|slippage_bps\" scripts/backtest_xsec_momentum.py"}, "routed_to": null, "state": "queued", "terminal_reason": null, "what": "checklist E3: scripts/backtest_xsec_momentum.py was wired to execution_costs for SLIPPAGE (via the same per-rebalance turnover-cost mechanism as its existing fee), but FUNDING was deliberately left unwired. The harness holds WEIGHTS across a multi-symbol universe with rebalance-to-rebalance bookkeeping, not per-position entry/exit Trade objects, so there is no clean per-leg hold-duration to charge execution_costs' funding-window drag against. The book trades a crypto-perp universe (per its own docstring: \"crypto long/short, dollar-neutral\"), so funding IS a real, currently-unpriced cost. Needs either (a) a per-symbol position-duration tracker between rebalances so funding windows crossed can be computed per leg, or (b) an explicit, documented decision that funding is out of scope for this harness with a stated reason beyond \"not yet built\"."}
